You are given a directed graph represented by an adjacency list and two functions `part1_bfs` and `part2_bfs` that perform breadth-first search (BFS) traversal on the graph. The `part1_bfs` function calculates the sum of distances from a given node `u` to all other nodes in the graph, while the `part2_bfs` function marks the nodes visited during the BFS traversal.

